Article 2. For the purposes of this Law, "transfer of ownership of land and buildings" means the following acts:
(1) Assignment of the right to use land;
(2) Transfer of the right to use land, including sale, gift, and exchange;
(3) Purchase, sale, gift, and exchange of buildings.
The transfer of the right to use land as referred to in item (2) of the preceding paragraph shall not include the transfer of the right to land contractual management or the right to land management.
Where ownership of land and buildings is transferred by means of investment (as equity contribution) at appraised value, debt repayment, transfer, award, or other means, deed tax shall be levied in accordance with the provisions of this Law.

Article 4. The basis for calculating deed tax shall be as follows:
(1) For assignment or sale of the right to use land, and for purchase and sale of buildings, the transaction price as determined in the contract for the transfer of ownership of the land and buildings, including the monetary amount payable and the price corresponding to the physical objects and other economic benefits;
(2) For exchange of the right to use land or exchange of buildings, the difference in price between the rights to use land or buildings exchanged;
(3) For gift of the right to use land or gift of buildings, and other transfers of ownership of land and buildings without a price, the price verified by the tax authority in accordance with the law by reference to the market price for the sale of the right to use land or the purchase and sale of buildings.
Where the transaction price or the price difference for exchange declared by the taxpayer is obviously low without a justifiable reason, the tax authority shall determine it in accordance with the provisions of the Law of the People's Republic of China on the Administration of Tax Collection.

Article 6. Deed tax shall be exempted in any of the following circumstances:
(1) State organs, institutions, social organizations, and military units acquire ownership of land and buildings for use in office, education, medical care, scientific research, or military facilities;
(2) Non-profit schools, medical institutions, and social welfare institutions acquire ownership of land and buildings for use in office, education, medical care, scientific research, elderly care, or relief;
(3) Acquisition of the right to use barren hills, barren land, or barren beaches for agricultural, forestry, animal husbandry, or fishery production;
(4) Changes in ownership of land and buildings between spouses during the existence of a marital relationship;
(5) Acquisition of ownership of land and buildings by statutory successors through succession;
(6) Acquisition of ownership of land and buildings by foreign embassies, consulates, and representative offices of international organizations in China that are entitled to tax exemption according to law.
Based on the needs of the national economy and social development, the State Council may provide for exemption or reduction of deed tax for circumstances such as ensuring housing needs of residents, restructuring and reorganization of enterprises, and post-disaster reconstruction, and shall report to the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress for record.
